Description: pvr: raise maxPushConstantsSize to 256 bytes
 maxPushConstantsSize is a literal 128, equal to PVR_MAX_PUSH_CONSTANTS_SIZE.
 The constant only sizes the CPU copy in struct pvr_push_constants
 (pvr_cmd_buffer.h). vkCmdPushConstants2 copies into it, the copy is uploaded
 as a buffer (pvr_cmd_upload_push_consts()) and the PDS descriptor program
 loads the range the shader reads into shared registers
 (PVR_BUFFER_TYPE_PUSH_CONSTS, pvr_setup_descriptors() in
 pvr_arch_pipeline.c). The DOUTD burst size field has 12 bits
 (PVR_ROGUE_PDSINST_DOUT_FIELDS_DOUTD_SRC1_BSIZE, pvr_rogue_pds_defs.h), so 64
 dwords fit in one burst.
 .
 Raise the constant to 256, the Vulkan 1.4 minimum, and report it. A shader
 that reads all of it uses 64 instead of 32 shared registers; vertex and
 fragment shaders have 1024 (ROGUE_MAX_VERTEX_SHARED_REGISTERS,
 ROGUE_MAX_PIXEL_SHARED_REGISTERS in rogue_hw_defs.h).
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
